  "status_text": "Keeping both answers costs exactly two more steps. Lean checked what happens when a new switch chooses between two different, nonconstant answers and one answer can only light up where the other does. Starting with both constants available, measure the smallest circuit that computes both answers. Keeping those answers and adding the switched output costs exactly two more gates, whether we use AND and OR alone or let NOT cost one gate. If we keep just one answer alongside that output, at least one extra gate is needed (L-lib-1163).",
